receding quarter's auction results, so I'll carefully examine the data files to find the specific 2-year Treasury note auction amounts.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_d9f7b1c5b9988dc7","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [ ] Identify Black Monday year and determine Q4 years needed\n- [ ] Find 2-year Treasury note auction data in available Treasury Bulletins\n- [ ] Extract Q4 auction amount tenders accepted for 1987, 1988, 1989, 1990\n- [ ] Calculate average for each Q4\n- [ ] Calculate slope of best-fit line through four Q4 averages\n- [ ] Report slope in millions of dollars per year (rounded)"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
