{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775255871-EVjIraQECvkMHNtVnbeG","role":"assistant","created":1775255875,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found the auction data. Let me search for more 2-year note auctions to understand the pattern. It looks like I need to find all Q4 (October, November, December) auctions for 2-year notes in each year and get the \"tenders accepted\" amount.\n\nLet me look at the full data more systematically. I need:\n- Q4 1987 (October, November, December 1987) - for 1988 bulletin\n- Q4 1988 (October, November, December 1988) - for 1989 bulletin\n- Q4 1989 (October, November, December 1989) - for 1990 bulletin\n- Q4 1990 (October, November, December 1990) - for 1991 bulletin\n\nLooking at the data found for 1987 (from 1988 bulletin):\n- October 14 auction: $9,255 million accepted\n- November 18 auction: $9,269 million accepted  \n- December 22 auction: $9,286 million accepted\n\nThese are the 2-year note auction tenders accepted. Let me find similar data for the other years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_37f5a75f43011793","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -A5 \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1988_03.txt | head -80"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_071e069e-6325-43a9-871c-c30350f8cefa","role":"user","created":1775255875,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_37f5a75f43011793","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Auction of 2-Year Notes\n\nOn October 14 the Treasury announced that it would auction $9,250 million of 2-year notes to refund $9,120 million of notes maturing October 31, 1987, and to raise about $125 million of new cash. The notes offered were Treasury Notes of Series AE-1989, dated November 2, 1987, due October 31, 1989, with interest payable on April 30 and October 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-7/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\n\nTenders for the notes were received until 1 p.m. EDST, October 21, and totaled $22,922 million, of which $9,255 million was accepted at yields ranging from 7.91 percent, price 99.937, up to 8.00 percent, price 99.774. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 8 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 7.95 percent, price 99.864. These totaled $768 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $8,487 million.\n\n--\nAuction of 2-Year Notes\n\nOn November 12 the Treasury announced that it would auction $9,250 million of 2-year notes of Series AF-1989 to refund $9,841 million of publicly held 2-year notes maturing November 30, 1987, and to pay down about $600 million.\n\nThe notes of Series AF-1989 were dated November 30, 1987, due November 30, 1989, with interest payable on May 31 and November 30 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-3/4 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\n","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"Auction of 2-Year Notes\n\nOn October 14 the Treasury announced that it would auction $9,250 million of 2-year notes to refund $9,120 million of notes maturing October 31, 1987, and to raise about $125 million of new cash. The notes offered were Treasury Notes of Series AE-1989, dated November 2, 1987, due October 31, 1989, with interest payable on April 30 and October 31 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-7/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\n\nTenders for the notes were received until 1 p.m. EDST, October 21, and totaled $22,922 million, of which $9,255 million was accepted at yields ranging from 7.91 percent, price 99.937, up to 8.00 percent, price 99.774. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 8 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 7.95 percent, price 99.864. These totaled $768 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $8,487 million.\n\n--\nAuction of 2-Year Notes\n\nOn November 12 the Treasury announced that it would auction $9,250 million of 2-year notes of Series AF-1989 to refund $9,841 million of publicly held 2-year notes maturing November 30, 1987, and to pay down about $600 million.\n\nThe notes of Series AF-1989 were dated November 30, 1987, due November 30, 1989, with interest payable on May 31 and November 30 until maturity. An interest rate of 7-3/4 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\n","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
