{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775255911-WY2Av2QK2Dziou1I4aQp","role":"assistant","created":1775255916,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to look at each file more systematically. Let me search for all \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\" entries in each file to find the Q4 auctions. The Q4 (October-November-December) auctions for each year would be:\n\n- 1987 (Q4 1987): October, November, December 1987\n- 1988 (Q4 1988): October, November, December 1988\n- 1989 (Q4 1989): October, November, December 1989\n- 1990 (Q4 1990): October, November, December 1990\n\nLet me extract all the 2-year note auction data from each file. Looking at the 1988 bulletin which covers Oct-Dec 1987:\n- October 21, 1987: $9,255 million accepted\n- November 18, 1987: $9,269 million accepted  \n- December 22, 1987: $9,286 million accepted\n\nNow let me check the 1989 bulletin which should cover Oct-Dec 1988.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ed4dfb1b27bd6c47","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -B5 \"2-Year Notes\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1989_03.txt | grep -E \"October|November|December|accepted|million\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_e67d5f98-6703-4281-be55-115204823b32","role":"user","created":1775255916,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_ed4dfb1b27bd6c47","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"On October 5 the Treasury announced that it would auction $6,750 million of 7-year notes to refund $3,198 million of notes maturing October 15, 1988, and to raise about $3,550 million of new cash. The notes offered were Treasury Notes of Series H-1995, dated October 17, 1988, due October 15, 1995, with interest payable on April 15 and October 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 8-5/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\nTenders for the notes were received until 1 p.m. EDST, October 12, 1988, and totaled $16,138 million, of which $6,754 million was accepted at yields ranging from 8.72 percent, price 99.510, up to 8.75 percent, price 99.356. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 61 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 8.73 percent, price 99.459. These totaled $306 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $6,448 million.","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"On October 5 the Treasury announced that it would auction $6,750 million of 7-year notes to refund $3,198 million of notes maturing October 15, 1988, and to raise about $3,550 million of new cash. The notes offered were Treasury Notes of Series H-1995, dated October 17, 1988, due October 15, 1995, with interest payable on April 15 and October 15 until maturity. An interest rate of 8-5/8 percent was set after the determination as to which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\nTenders for the notes were received until 1 p.m. EDST, October 12, 1988, and totaled $16,138 million, of which $6,754 million was accepted at yields ranging from 8.72 percent, price 99.510, up to 8.75 percent, price 99.356. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 61 percent. Noncompetitive tenders were accepted in full at the average yield, 8.73 percent, price 99.459. These totaled $306 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $6,448 million.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
