g by the denominator of 5 yields 1015.60.\n\nThis converts to 1016 million per year. The calculation checks out.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_7290a5a18c958c98","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Identify Black Monday year and determine Q4 years needed\n- [x] Find 2-year Treasury note auction data in available Treasury Bulletins\n- [x] Extract Q4 auction amount tenders accepted for 1987, 1988, 1989, 1990\n- [x] Calculate average for each Q4\n- [x] Calculate slope of best-fit line through four Q4 averages\n- [x] Report slope in millions of dollars per year (rounded)"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
